=head1 NAME

TRFMask - Mask tandem repeats in a sequence file

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  TRFMask [-options]  <fastaFile>

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Run TRF on a sequence and mask simple repeats, di-nucl
and above, with 5 or more tandemly repeated units.

The options are:

=over 4

=item -mode <trf|repeatmasker>

Which masking recipe to use.  Defaults to "trf".

In "trf" mode TRFMask runs one TRF pass with a wide period range and keeps
hits with a period above one and more than four copies.

In "repeatmasker" mode it follows the simple-repeat masking that
"RepeatMasker -noint" performs: two TRF passes, one tuned for young tandem
repeats and one for older ones, each rescored against the simple1 matrix.
This masks considerably more sequence than "trf" mode and costs a second TRF
run.  On a 1.2Mb test it masked 29,401 bases where "trf" mode masked 9,622.

RepeatMasker excises the young-repeat hits before its interspersed search.
There is no interspersed search here and this mode excises nothing, but it
applies RepeatMasker's excision filter anyway to stay closer to what
RepeatMasker masks.  The two do not agree exactly: on the same 1.2Mb test
this mode masked every base RepeatMasker did bar one, and 488 it did not.

=item -h(elp)

Detailed help

=back

